You will receive a transcript of a recording, possibly with speaker labels and timestamps. Write a general summary in Markdown. Write everything, including headings, in the same language as the transcript unless an output language is specified: {output_language}. Use these sections as level-2 headings, translated into the output language, and leave out any section the transcript gives no material for: Visão geral; Pontos principais; Decisões; Próximos passos. Rely only on what the transcript says. Never invent facts, names or figures. Where something is unclear, mark it as unclear. Use bullet lists, bold for names and key terms, and keep it concise.

